+## Live Instrument
+
+When Obsidian is running, the `obsidian` CLI drives this loop against the live app, so each step reads the rendered result instead of the CSS you hoped for:
+
+```bash
+obsidian dev:screenshot path=<file>                                 # capture the window
+obsidian dev:css selector=".workspace-leaf" prop=background-color   # winning rules, with source lines
+obsidian dev:dom selector=".workspace-tab-header" total             # confirm the object exists
+obsidian reload                                                     # reload the vault after a snippet edit
+obsidian dev:console level=error                                    # snippet parse errors
+```
+
+Two of these change how the loop behaves. `dev:screenshot` captures Obsidian's own window whether or not it is frontmost, which removes occlusion and the need to verify the verifier. `dev:css` reports which rule actually won and where it came from, which turns "nothing changed" from a guess into a lookup.
+
+The CLI needs Obsidian running with `cli` enabled in Settings > General > Advanced. Without it, fall back to reading `.obsidian/` files and `screencapture`. The loop is the same; only the instrument changes.
+
